          #s4.question-answer._column-span-all
            h4.question
              | Q: Can I search by
              a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://varnomen.hgvs.org/') HGVS description
              | (e.g. ALDH2:p.Glu504Lys)?
            .answer
              p
                | Yes. HGVSc (e.g.
                a(target='_blank', href='/?term=ALDH2%3Ac.1510G%3EA') ALDH2:c.1510G&gt;A
                | ) and HGVSp (e.g.
                a(target='_blank', href='/?term=ALDH2%3Ap.Glu504Lys') ALDH2:p.Glu504Lys
                | ) are acceptable.
                |
                a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://m.ensembl.org/info/docs/tools/vep/recoder/index.html') Variant Recoder
                | is used to convert an HGVS description to a GRCh38/GRCh37 position.
          #s5.question-answer._column-span-all
            h4.question
              | Q: What can I do with the
              |
              a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='/?mode=advanced') Advanced search
              | ?
            .answer
              p
                |You can build a query with an alternate allele frequency, clinical significance,
                | and other search criteria combined with the AND and/or OR operator. See
                a.link(href='#s6') "Q: Can I search for variants with higher alternate allele frequencies in Japanese populations than in other populations?"
                |
                |for usage.
          #s6.question-answer._column-span-all
            h4.question Can I search for variants with higher alternate allele frequencies in Japanese populations than in other populations?
            .answer
              p
                | Yes. Use
                a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://grch37.togovar.org/?mode=advanced') Advanced search
                | .
              p.body
                | The following example uses the GRCh37 version of the site (
                a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://grch37.togovar.org/') grch37.togovar.org
                | ). ToMMo 8.3KJPN is a dataset included in the GRCh37 version.
              p
                | Variant sets for comparison of alternate allele frequencies are as follows:
              .document-block
                ul.unordered-list
                  li For Japanese populations, variants included in either GEM-J WGA or ToMMo 8.3KJPN
                  li For other populations, variants included in either gnomAD genomes or gnomAD exomes
              p
                | This example searches for variants with an alternate allele frequency of at least 0.3 in Japanese populations and at most 0.05 in gnomAD populations.
              ol.ordered-list
                li Select the Advanced search tab at the top of the
                  a.hyper-text.-external(target='_blank', href='https://grch37.togovar.org/')  GRCh37 home page
                  img(src=require("../../../images/help-image1.png") alt="Selecting the Advanced search tab")
                li Select Alternate allele frequency/count from the Add condition menu.
                  p
                    img(src=require("../../../images/help-image2.png") alt="Selecting Alternate allele frequency/count" width="241")
                li Specify GEM-J WGA and an alternate allele frequency of at least 0.3. You can also specify the number of alternate alleles.
                  img(src=require("../../../images/help-image3.png") alt="Specifying a dataset and alternate allele frequency")
                li Click OK to set the search condition.
                  img(src=require("../../../images/help-image4.png") alt="Setting a search condition")
                li In the same way, set conditions for ToMMo 8.3KJPN, gnomAD genomes, and gnomAD exomes.
                  img(src=require("../../../images/help-image5.png") alt="Conditions for each dataset")
                li Combine the Japanese population conditions for GEM-J WGA and ToMMo 8.3KJPN with OR.
                  ol.ordered-list
                    li Select the GEM-J WGA and ToMMo 8.3KJPN conditions. Selected conditions are enclosed by yellow borders.
                      img(src=require("../../../images/help-image6.png") alt="Selecting Japanese population conditions")
                    li Select the Group menu. The two selected conditions are combined with OR. To change it to AND, click the OR icon on the left.
                      img(src=require("../../../images/help-image7.png") alt="Combining conditions with OR")
                    li Combine the gnomAD genomes and gnomAD exomes conditions with OR in the same way.
                      img(src=require("../../../images/help-image8.png") alt="Combining gnomAD conditions with OR")
              p The final search criteria are as follows:
              pre.document-block.-code.
                ((freq(GEM-J WGA) >= 0.3) OR (freq(ToMMo 8.3KJPN) >= 0.3))
                AND
                ((freq(gnomAD genomes) <= 0.05) OR (freq(gnomAD exomes) <= 0.05))
              p
                | Each time search criteria is changed, the search is automatically executed and a list of variants that match the criteria is refreshed.
              img(src=require("../../../images/help-image9.webp") alt="Search results and search conditions")
              p Functions in the menu bar
              ul.unordered-list
                li Add condition: Add search criteria to the query builder.
                li Group: Combine selected search criteria with OR. Click the OR icon to change it to AND.
                li Ungroup: Separate grouped search criteria.
                li Delete: Delete selected search criteria.
              p Meaning of the icons
              ul.unordered-list
                li
                  img(src=require("../../../images/help-pencil.png") alt="Edit search criteria icon" width="24" height="24")
                  | : Edit search criteria.
                li
                  img(src=require("../../../images/help-cross.png") alt="Delete search criteria icon" width="24" height="24")
                  | : Delete search criteria.
          #s7.question-answer._column-span-all
            h4.question Can I search for variants by both positions on GRCh38 and GRCh37?
            .answer
              p
                | Yes. The reference assembly is shown in the header. Click it to switch between GRCh37 and GRCh38.
              img(src=require("../../../images/help-image10.png") alt="Switching the reference assembly" width="600")
